# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://dv-flow.github.io/flow.dv.schema.json
package:
  name: hdltest.svunit
  desc: SVUnit unit tests, built and run by any hdlsim simulator
  doc: |
    Runs SVUnit tests through `hdlsim`, without SVUnit's `runSVUnit` script.
    SVUnit's scripts generate glue (one test suite per directory, plus a
    `testrunner` top) and then call the simulator themselves. Here the glue is
    generated by a task, and compiling and running are ordinary
    `hdlsim.<sim>.SimImage` and `SimRun` tasks. So:
    * any simulator hdlsim supports runs the tests;
    * the DUT's sources come from whatever tasks already produce them;
    * the verdict is an `hdlsim.TestResult` that rolls up in a
      `hdlsim.SimSuiteReport` with every other test.

    Test files are unchanged SVUnit: each is a `module <name>_unit_test` using
    the usual `SVTEST` macros.

    ```
    svunitTest files ─► TestRunner ─┐
                   Lib (SVUnit) ────┼─► hdlsim.<sim>.SimImage (top: testrunner) ─► SimRun (mode: test) ─► Check ─► hdlsim.TestResult
            DUT sources ────────────┘
    ```

    ```yaml
    - name: svunit
      uses: hdltest.svunit.Lib
    - name: tests
      uses: std.FileSet
      with: {type: svunitTest, include: ["*_unit_test.sv"]}
    - name: runner
      uses: hdltest.svunit.TestRunner
      needs: [tests]
    - name: img
      uses: hdlsim.vlt.SimImage
      needs: [svunit, dut, runner]
      with: {top: [testrunner]}
    - name: run
      uses: hdlsim.vlt.SimRun
      needs: [img]
      with: {mode: test}
    - name: check
      uses: hdltest.svunit.Check
      needs: [run]
      with: {gate: true}
    ```

    **File type** `svunitTest`: an SVUnit unit-test file, one or more
    `module <name>_unit_test` declarations. It is kept apart from
    `systemVerilogSource` so that the runner knows which modules to collect.

    **Finding SVUnit** (`Lib`), in order:
    1. the `install` parameter;
    2. `$SVUNIT_INSTALL`, SVUnit's own convention, so an existing install works
       unchanged;
    3. `$IVPM_PACKAGES/svunit`, the copy IVPM fetches for a project that depends
       on dv-flow-libhdltest (pinned in this package's `ivpm.yaml`);
    4. `packages/svunit` under the root package's directory or any parent.

    A location given by 1 or 2 that is not an SVUnit install is an error; the
    search does not fall through to another copy.

    Not supported yet: SVUnit's UVM mode (`RUN_SVUNIT_WITH_UVM`), its
    experimental self-registering tests, and `_type_test` modules.

  imports:
  - hdlsim

  tasks:
  - name: Lib
    desc: Find SVUnit and provide its package sources to the simulator
    doc: |
      Output -- one `systemVerilogSource` fileset: `junit_xml.sv` and
      `svunit_pkg.sv`, with `svunit_base` and `svunit_base/junit-xml` on the
      include path. The package doc says where SVUnit is looked for.

      **verilator_compat** (on by default). Verilator v5.048 and later reject
      SVUnit's `svunit_testsuite` class ("Duplicate declaration of VARSCOPE
      ... i__Vloopsize"). With this set, `Lib` stages a copy of `svunit_base`
      in its run directory with one `foreach` loop variable renamed. The
      rename changes no behaviour on any simulator, and it is only applied
      when the SVUnit source has the affected loop.
    with:
      install:
        doc: SVUnit installation directory (the one holding svunit_base/). Default -- searched for.
        type: str
        value: ""
      verilator_compat:
        doc: Stage a copy of svunit_base with the rename Verilator 5.050+ needs
        type: bool
        value: true
    shell: pytask
    run: dv_flow.libhdltest.svunit.lib.Lib

  - name: TestRunner
    desc: Generate SVUnit's test suites and test runner for the unit-test files
    doc: |
      Consumes `svunitTest` filesets. Each fileset becomes one test suite
      (SVUnit's own scripts make one per directory), named after the task that
      produced it. Every `module <name>_unit_test` in its files becomes a test
      case of that suite.

      Outputs, in compile order:
      * the unit-test files, as `systemVerilogSource`, each fileset with its own
        directory on the include path;
      * one `systemVerilogSource` fileset of generated files:
        `<suite>_testsuite.sv` for each suite, then `<top>.sv`.

      Set the simulator's top to `top` (`testrunner` by default). The
      generated code matches what SVUnit's `create_testsuite.pl` and
      `create_testrunner.pl` write, minus the UVM and self-registration hooks.

      **harness** lists modules (no ports) that the test runner instantiates
      beside the suites: a test bench the unit tests share, such as the
      clock, the design and its transactors. The unit tests reach it through
      a package or by hierarchical name. Swapping the file that defines a
      harness module swaps the bench without touching a test: for example,
      the same tests against a model and against RTL.
    consumes:
    - filetype: svunitTest
    with:
      top:
        doc: Name of the generated test-runner module (the simulation top)
        type: str
        value: testrunner
      harness:
        doc: Modules to instantiate in the test runner, beside the suites
        type: list
        value: []
    shell: pytask
    run: dv_flow.libhdltest.svunit.runner.TestRunner

  - name: Check
    desc: Turn an SVUnit simulation log into a pass/fail hdlsim.TestResult
    doc: |
      Consumes the `hdlsim.SimRunResult` of a `SimRun` (use `mode: test`, so
      a failing run does not stop the flow), and produces an
      `hdlsim.TestResult`.

      SVUnit exits 0 whether its tests pass or not, so the verdict comes from
      the log:
      * `pass` -- the runner reports PASSED and no test failed;
      * `fail` -- the runner reports FAILED;
      * `error` -- the run ended before the runner's report (a crash,
        `$fatal`, or timeout), or exited nonzero.

      Each failed check (`ERROR: ... (at <file> line:<n>)`) becomes a marker at
      that line of the unit-test file. The TestResult's `stats` carry
      `tests_run`, `tests_passed`, `tests_failed`, `suites` and
      `suites_passing`. SVUnit's own JUnit report (`tests.xml`) is forwarded
      as a `junitXml` artifact.

      **gate**. With `gate: false` (the default, as `hdlsim.SimCheck`), a
      failure is data: the markers are informational and the task succeeds,
      so a suite keeps running and `hdlsim.SimSuiteReport` is the gate. With
      `gate: true`, failures are error markers and the task fails. Use it when
      the check is the end of the flow.
    consumes:
    - type: hdlsim.SimRunResult
    produces:
    - type: hdlsim.TestResult
    uptodate: false
    with:
      name:
        doc: Case name recorded in the TestResult. Default -- the run directory's name.
        type: str
        value: ""
      testname:
        doc: Test identity recorded in the TestResult
        type: str
        value: svunit
      gate:
        doc: Fail the task (with error markers) when the tests do not pass
        type: bool
        value: false
    shell: pytask
    run: dv_flow.libhdltest.svunit.check.Check
